# Delegator board — read it, append to it

**Always on for this workspace.** Companion doc: `00_docs/agent/DELEGATOR_BOARD.md`.

There is no message channel between agents on this machine — Cursor exposes no tool for one agent
to ping another. The board is the substitute. It is how the next agent learns what the last one
changed.

## At the start of a substantive run

Read the last ~10 rows of `00_docs/agent/DELEGATOR_BOARD.md`. If a recent row names a file you are
about to touch, that file changed recently — check what moved before building on it.

## When you finish a substantive piece of work

Append one line:

```
| YYYY-MM-DD HH:mm | <your agent name> | <what changed, one clause> | <files you wrote> | <next step, or None> |
```

One line. This is a change log, not a report — the detail belongs in the file you wrote.

## When the board says AIM moved

Read `00_docs/agent/DELEGATOR_REFRESH_HOWTO.md` before doing anything. The pricing deliverables it
lists are **locked read-only** (Jerome, 2026-09-17). New work goes to new dated files.

## Do not

- Do not write to the locked pricing deliverables listed in the howto.
- Do not treat a board row as permission to rebuild, publish, or move a price.
- Do not paste reports into the board.
